# Documentation Sync on Infrastructure Change

When infrastructure behavior changes, documentation must be updated in the same work session.

## Required updates

- Update runbooks such as `docs/it/mcp-consumer.md` (Atlas Model Context Protocol consumer) when endpoint contracts, bearer auth, or deployment wiring change. Sibling Graphics Processing Unit (GPU) / RunPod ops live in `atlas-mcp-server/Runpod_VM.md`.
- Update environment variable guidance in `env.template`, README, or Information Technology (IT) runbooks when endpoint contracts change.
- Record newly observed operational failure signatures and resolutions in troubleshooting sections (`docs/it/commissioning.md` and deep appendix).

## Completion rule

Do not consider infrastructure work complete until documentation reflects the latest known-good working state.
